wow, you guessed right!
I actually first found out that running NetHack through GDB left me an
empty record file, so I imagined I should be placed in the HACKDIR and
that worked :D

>
> I have the following in my ~/.gdbinit:
>
> define nhdebug
> =A0 set args -D
> =A0 set environment HACKDIR ./
> =A0 file nethack
> =A0 run
> end
>
> And then I can just use that command, for example with
> =A0"gdb --eval-command=3Dnhdebug"
> when I'm in the NetHack playground dir.

